  "published": "2026-10-31T20:52:23.567Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0:\n- Fix: pipeline behaviors now run in registration order, as documented and as in MediatR. The first registered behavior is the outermost. Previously the last registered ran first. Exception handler/action wrappers stay outermost and pre/post-processor wrappers stay innermost. Review the order of AddOpenBehavior calls if you registered more than one behavior.\n- RequestHandlerDelegate and StreamHandlerDelegate take an optional CancellationToken, so behaviors written for MediatR can call next() without arguments.\n- Send and CreateStream throw an InvalidOperationException that names the request, the handler interface to implement and the registration call to add when no handler is registered.\n- XML documentation for the whole public API, shipped in the package for IntelliSense and coding assistants.\n- Package metadata: documentation site as project URL, MediatR-alternative description and tags.\n- New documentation site: https://adiakys.github.io/OpenMediator/",
